    <section class="block-background rich-text-block blockpadding-top--default   textcolor--dark textalign--left"  data-id="74978fce-946f-494b-bdbd-72a20d0c7701" >
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12 title-content">
                        <div class="title-content__title">
                            
<div style="text-align: center;">
<h5 style="background-color: #29389a; color: #ffffff; padding: 15px 20px; border-radius: 10px; text-align: center;">For the latest updates on the Cloud Backup service interruption, <a href="#cloudbackup" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline;">click here</a>.</h5>
</div>

                        </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section> 
<style> 
[data-id='74978fce-946f-494b-bdbd-72a20d0c7701'] {
--background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);
}</style>

    <section class="block-background rich-text-block blockpadding-top--small blockpadding-bottom--default  textcolor--dark textalign--left"  data-id="0ba735a9-bdb9-4832-af29-90aea132086d" >
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12 title-content">
                        <div class="title-content__title">
                            
<h1>Latest Advisories</h1>

                        </div>
                        <div class="title-content__rich-text rich-text">
                            
<p><em>From time to time, ConnectWise will provide communications on broader security related topics that may not be linked to a specific ConnectWise product or vulnerability, but are still of importance to our partner community.</em></p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<h2>October 22, 2026: Axcient Legacy Portal service restored</h2>
<p><span style="font-size: 16px;"><strong>The Backup for Files Portal (Legacy Portal) has been fully restored and is operational</strong> following remediation of the industry-wide PHP vulnerabilities.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 16px;">All Axcient backup services remain operational, and backups continued running throughout the portal interruption.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 16px;">This issue was separate from the Cloud Backup incident.</span></p>
<p>The broader industry issue involves two critical vulnerabilities in PHP, a technology widely used in websites, applications and management portals. The <a aria-label="Link official PHP security advisory" id="menur4bk0" href="https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php">official PHP security advisory</a> warns that the vulnerabilities could allow unauthorized code execution and urges immediate security updates. Partners should review their own and their customers&rsquo; applications and portals for affected PHP components and follow the advisory and their software vendors&rsquo; guidance.</p>
<p>Thank you for your patience while we completed this work. Contact Partner Care if you need assistance accessing the portal.</p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<h2>October 21, 2026: Axcient security and portal availability update</h2>
<p>In response to the industry-wide PHP vulnerabilities, <strong>we have completed remediation for Axcient x360Recover.</strong></p>
<p><strong>The Backup for Files Portal (Legacy Portal) remains temporarily offline while mitigation work continues, affecting a small number of partners using legacy products.</strong></p>
<p><strong>All Axcient backup services remain operational, and backups continue running. This action is separate from the Cloud Backup incident.</strong></p>
<p>The broader industry issue involves two critical vulnerabilities in PHP, a technology widely used in websites, applications, and management portals. The <a href="https://www.php.net/archive/2026.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official PHP security advisory</a> warns that the vulnerabilities could allow unauthorized code execution and urges immediate security updates. Partners should review their own and their customers' applications and portals for affected PHP components and follow the advisory and their software vendors' guidance.</p>
<p>We will provide further information as it becomes available.</p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<h2 id="cloudbackup">October 26, 2026: Cloud Backup (formerly known as SkyKick) Service Interruption</h2>
<p><em>This advisory was originally published on October 16 at 17:47 UTC and last updated on October 26 at 14:00 UTC.<br /><br />See <a href="#faqs">FAQs below</a> for further information.</em></p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-26-1400-utc"><strong style="color: #24326a;">Update: Monday, October 26, 2026 at 14:00 UTC</strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup investigation and restoration update</strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists continue restoration, testing and security validation.</p>
<p><strong>We continue preparing for phased partner onboarding and will provide an update as soon as partners can begin restoring data from existing backups.</strong></p>
<h6><strong>What partners can expect</strong></h6>

<ol>
<li><strong>Backup restoration access first.</strong> We are first enabling a process for partners to restore data from existing backups.</li>
<li><strong>Full service re-enrollment to follow.</strong> We will then begin phased re-enrollment, supported by step-by-step instructions, video tutorials and webinars to help partners re-establish service and verify successful operation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Previously published findings and partner guidance remain current. <strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until ConnectWise provides instructions that apply to your service.</strong> Infrastructure restoration does not mean all partner capabilities are available. We will share confirmed availability and any changes to anticipated timing through the Trust Center.</p>
<p>Investigation and monitoring continue alongside restoration. Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated and preserved, with no indication of compromise. We have no indication that other ConnectWise products, services or offerings are impacted by this incident.</p>
<p>Reviewing individual Microsoft 365 environments remains essential. Continue using the <a href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and <a href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" title="https://www.connectwise.com/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation">technical webinars</a> for your own and managed customer environments.</p>
<p>We recognize the continued disruption to your business and customers and remain focused on restoring service safely.</p>
<p><strong>Our next daily update will be published by October 27 at 14:00 UTC. We will communicate significant developments sooner.</strong></p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-25-1400-utc"><strong style="color: #24326a;">Update: Sunday, October 25, 2026 at 14:00 UTC</strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup investigation and restoration update</strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists continue restoration, testing and security validation,<strong> with phased partner onboarding targeted for Monday, October 26.</strong></p>
<h6><strong>What partners can expect</strong></h6>
<ol>
<li><strong>Backup restoration access first.</strong> We anticipate enabling a process for partners to restore data from existing backups Monday, following successful testing and validation.</li>
<li><strong>Full service re-enrollment to follow.</strong> We will then begin phased re-enrollment, supported by step-by-step instructions, video tutorials and webinars to help partners re-establish service and verify successful operation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Previously published findings and partner guidance remain current. <strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until ConnectWise provides instructions that apply to your service.</strong> Infrastructure restoration does not mean all partner capabilities are available. We will share confirmed availability and any changes to anticipated timing through the Trust Center.</p>
<p>Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated and preserved, with no indication of compromise. We have no indication that other ConnectWise products, services or offerings are impacted by this incident.</p>
<p>Reviewing individual Microsoft 365 environments remains essential. Continue using the <a href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and <a href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" title="https://www.connectwise.com/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation">technical webinars</a> for your own and managed customer environments.</p>
<p>We recognize the continued disruption to your business and customers and remain focused on restoring service safely.</p>
<p><strong>Our next daily update will be published by October 26 at 14:00 UTC. We will communicate significant developments sooner.</strong></p>
<p>Visit the <a href="/company/trust/advisories" title="https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories">ConnectWise Trust Center</a> for current status and guidance. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to <a href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" title="mailto:securitypartnersupport@connectwise.com">SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</a>.</p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<p><strong style="color: #24326a;"></strong></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-24-1400-utc"><strong style="color: #24326a;">Update: Saturday, October 24, 2026 at 14:00 UTC</strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup investigation and restoration update</strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists are bringing services back online in a controlled sequence, including rotating certificates across our infrastructure.</p>
<p><strong>Restoration, testing and security validation will continue through the weekend, with a target of beginning phased partner onboarding on Monday, October 26, subject to successful completion of the required checks.</strong></p>
<h6><strong>What partners can expect</strong></h6>
<ol>
<li><strong>Backup restoration access first.</strong> We anticipate enabling a process for partners to restore data from existing backups Monday, following successful testing and validation.</li>
<li><strong>Full service re-enrollment to follow.</strong> We will then begin phased re-enrollment, supported by step-by-step instructions, video tutorials and webinars to help partners re-establish service and verify successful operation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Previously published findings and partner guidance remain current.</p>
<p><strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until ConnectWise provides instructions that apply to your service.</strong> Bringing infrastructure online does not mean all partner capabilities are available. We will share confirmed availability and any changes to anticipated timing through the Trust Center.</p>
<p>Investigation and monitoring continue alongside restoration. Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated and preserved, with no indication of compromise. We have no indication that other ConnectWise products, services or offerings are impacted by this incident.</p>
<p>Reviewing individual Microsoft 365 environments remains essential. Continue using the <a href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and <a href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technical webinars</a> for your own and managed customer environments.</p>
<p>We recognize the continued disruption to your business and customers and remain focused on restoring service safely.</p>
<p><strong>Our next daily update will be published by October 25 at 14:00 UTC. We will communicate significant developments sooner.</strong></p>
<p>Visit the <a href="/company/trust/advisories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ConnectWise Trust Center</a> for current status and guidance. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to <a href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com">SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</a>.</p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-23-1400-utc"><strong style="color: #24326a;">Update: Friday, October 23, 2026 at 14:00 UTC</strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup investigation and restoration update</strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists continue restoration testing and security validation.</p>
<p><strong>We anticipate completing this work by the end of this weekend.</strong> Successful completion will allow us to begin returning capabilities to partners in phases.</p>
<h6><strong>What partners can expect</strong></h6>
<ol>
<li><strong>Backup restoration access first.</strong> We anticipate enabling a process for partners to restore data from existing backups early next week, following successful testing and validation.</li>
<li><strong>Full service re-enrollment to follow.</strong> Phased re-enrollment will be supported by step-by-step instructions, video tutorials and webinars to help partners re-establish service and verify successful operation.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until ConnectWise provides instructions that apply to your service.</strong> We will share confirmed availability and any changes to anticipated timing through the Trust Center.</p>
<p>Investigation and monitoring continue alongside restoration. Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated and preserved, with no indication of compromise. We have no indication that other ConnectWise products, services or offerings are impacted by this incident.</p>
<p>Reviewing individual Microsoft 365 environments remains essential. Continue using the <a href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and <a href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technical webinars</a> for your own and managed customer environments.</p>
<p>We recognize the continued disruption to your business and customers and remain focused on restoring service safely.</p>
<p><strong>We will publish updates once daily at 14:00 UTC, with significant developments shared sooner. Our next update will be published by October 24 at 14:00 UTC.</strong></p>
