<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-21-2200-utc"><strong style="color: #24326a;">Update: Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 22:00 UTC</strong></p>
<h6><strong>ConnectWise Cloud Backup Update: What we know about the attacker and what it means for partners</strong></h6>
<p>Based on the evidence available to ConnectWise, including threat intelligence shared by Microsoft, it appears that a China state-aligned group was responsible for the attack on ConnectWise Cloud Backup. The group used an openly available agentic AI framework to automate and speed up its operation.</p>
<p>Microsoft's <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/21/storm-0940-uses-artex-agentic-ai-connectwise-supply-chain-compromise/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">research</a> describes a campaign that reaches well beyond any one company. This group has been active since 2021, and since at least September it has used the same AI tooling against organizations in aerospace and defense, energy, financial services, government, legal, manufacturing, semiconductors and technology. Microsoft also reports that threat actors in multiple regions are now using the same framework, and that in several cases attackers reached privileged cloud access in under three hours.</p>
<p>Nation-state actors are increasingly targeting the software supply chain, because one trusted connection can open the door to many organizations. AI now lets them test those connections at what Microsoft calls 'machine speed'. MSPs are in the middle of that chain. They are targets in their own right, and they are also a path into every client they serve. Every vendor and every MSP must defend itself with both of those risks in mind, and we intend to share what we are learning from this incident so our partners can do that.</p>
<p>Our first responsibility is to our partners. We contained the affected application connections and are restoring services in controlled phases. Those actions do not remove unauthorized access that may already have been established within individual customer tenants, which require separate review. We are also working with independent specialists so partners have the evidence they need to review their own tenants. Partners should keep affected connections disabled until we issue formal instructions, and should follow the current guidance on the <a href="/company/trust/advisories#cloudbackup">ConnectWise Trust Center.</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-21-1900-utc"><strong><span style="color: #24326a;">Update: Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 19:00 UTC</span></strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update</strong><strong></strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p><strong>We have begun restoring services in controlled phases, following remediation and security validation.</strong></p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists continue validating the affected environment, with each restoration step subject to security review. We expect the process to take several days; the start of restoration does not mean all capabilities are available.</p>
<p>We will share service-specific availability and step-by-step reconnection instructions as they are confirmed. <strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until formal instructions apply to your service.</strong></p>
<p>Our investigation continues alongside restoration. Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated, and preserved, with no indication of compromise. These findings do not establish whether individual partner or customer Microsoft 365 tenants were affected. We continue monitoring our broader environment, with no indication that other ConnectWise products, services, or offerings are impacted by this incident.</p>
<p>Please continue using the <a aria-label="Link technical investigation and remediation guide" id="menur24op" href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and <a aria-label="Link technical webinars" id="menur24os" href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation">technical webinars</a> to review your own and managed customer tenants.&nbsp;Additionally, a list of ConnectWise public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses is <a href="https://docs.connectwise.com/ConnectWise_Business_Knowledge/200/Connectwise_Public_IP_Addresses">available here</a> for reference.</p>
<p>We recognize the continued disruption and remain responsible for supporting you and restoring service safely. Visit the <a aria-label="Link Trust Center" id="menur24ov" href="/company/trust/advisories" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories">Trust Center</a> for updates. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to <a aria-label="Link SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" id="menur24p2" href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="mailto:securitypartnersupport@connectwise.com">SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</a>.</p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-21-1245-utc"><strong><span style="color: #24326a;"><br />Update: Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 12:45 UTC</span></strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update</strong></h6>
<p>As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application credentials associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</p>
<p><strong>We have begun restoring services in controlled phases, following remediation and security validation.</strong></p>
<p>Our teams and independent specialists continue validating the affected environment, with each restoration step subject to security review.</p>
<p>We expect restoration to take several days. Service availability will return in stages, and the start of restoration does not mean all capabilities are available. We recognize the continued disruption to your business and customers and remain focused on restoring service safely.</p>
<h6><strong>Partner reconnection instructions</strong></h6>
<p>We will publish <strong>step-by-step instructions</strong> explaining when and how partners should reconnect affected services, including any required reauthorization and verification steps. <strong>Keep affected application connections disabled until ConnectWise provides formal instructions for your service.</strong></p>
<p>We will share service-specific availability and more precise restoration timing as they are confirmed.</p>
<h6><strong>Technical resources for partners</strong></h6>
<p>Reviewing individual Microsoft 365 environments remains essential as restoration progresses. Our <a aria-label="Link technical investigation and remediation guide" id="menurlif" href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> provides detailed steps for reviewing your own tenant and each managed customer tenant, including legacy SkyKick integrations.</p>
<p>Our <a aria-label="Link technical webinar series" id="menurlii" href="/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/webinars/cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation">technical webinar series</a> continues every two hours to help partners apply the guidance. Sessions provide hands-on walkthroughs of Microsoft Entra ID sign-in and audit logs, application registrations, credentials, and permissions. Please register for an upcoming session and share these resources with the administrators responsible for your customer environments.</p>
<p>Resellers, distributors, and marketplace partners should ensure this guidance reaches the responsible customer administrators.</p>
<h6><strong>Investigation and monitoring</strong></h6>
<p>Our investigation continues alongside restoration. Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated, and preserved, with no indication of compromise. These findings do not establish whether individual partner or customer Microsoft 365 environments were affected.</p>
<p>We continue monitoring our partner-facing services and broader environment around the clock, with no indication that other ConnectWise products, services, or offerings are impacted.</p>
<p><strong>Our next update will be published by October 21 at 19:00 UTC. We will communicate significant developments sooner as they are confirmed.</strong></p>
