<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-20-0045-utc"><strong><span style="color: #24326a;">Update: Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 00:45 UTC</span></strong></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update<br /></strong><br />As previously reported, we identified unauthorized access to application identities associated with Cloud Backup, formerly SkyKick.</h6>
<p>Our teams and third-party specialists continue advancing remediation and validating the affected environment for safe restoration. We have strengthened administrative-access protections and are resetting accounts and replacing application credentials within that environment.<strong> We take responsibility for keeping you informed and restoring service safely.</strong></p>
<h6><strong>Actions completed to date</strong></h6>
<ul>
<li>Disabled affected application connections and suspended Cloud Backup to protect partners and their customers.</li>
<li>Suspended SaaS Security and Cloud Management as a precaution because they are integrated with Cloud Backup.</li>
<li>Engaged independent third-party specialists to support the investigation and remediation.</li>
<li>Strengthened administrative-access protections.</li>
<li>Published technical guidance to help partners investigate and remediate potential unauthorized activity in their own and managed customer environments.</li>
</ul>
<h6><strong>Work underway and next steps</strong></h6>
<p>Validation of remediation and the effectiveness of our containment measures remains underway, supported by third-party forensics specialists. Our teams are monitoring our entire environment around the clock. Since mitigations began on October 17 at 05:00 UTC, we have not observed successful threat activity in the environments we monitor. This observation does not establish whether individual partner or customer Microsoft 365 tenants have been affected. Reviewing each potentially affected tenant remains essential.</p>
<p>At this time, we have no indication that ConnectWise products, services, or offerings beyond Cloud Backup and the precautionary suspensions of SaaS Security and Cloud Management are impacted.</p>
<p>We plan to restore services in controlled phases, subject to completion of the required remediation and security validation. Before services are re-enabled, we will provide clear instructions explaining any actions partners need to take.</p>
<h6><strong>Service availability and stored backups</strong></h6>
<p>Existing backup archives remain encrypted, isolated, and preserved, with no indication that they have been compromised. These findings concern stored archives and do not establish whether live Microsoft 365 environments were affected.</p>
<p>Cloud Backup, SaaS Security, and Cloud Management remain suspended. Scheduled backups, archive access, restores, SaaS Security monitoring and alerting, and Cloud Management user and license management remain unavailable. We recognize the disruption to your business and customers and will share restoration timing as soon as it is confirmed.</p>
<h6><strong>Actions for partners</strong></h6>
<p>Continue following the <a aria-label="Link technical investigation and remediation guide" id="menur6qk1" href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> and the accompanying step-by-step video below when reviewing your Microsoft 365 tenant and each managed customer tenant. Keep affected applications disabled pending formal restoration instructions.</p>
<p>Resellers, distributors, and marketplace partners should ensure this guidance reaches the responsible customer administrators.</p>
<p><strong>Our next update will be published by October 20 13:00 UTC. We will communicate significant developments as they are confirmed.</strong></p>
<p>Visit the <a aria-label="Link Trust Center" id="menur6qk4" href="/company/trust/advisories" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories">Trust Center</a> for updates. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to <a aria-label="Link SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" id="menur6qk7" href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="mailto:securitypartnersupport@connectwise.com">SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</a>.<br /><br /><br /></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-19-1850-utc"><strong><span style="color: #24326a;">Update: Monday, October 19, 2026 at 18:50 UTC</span></strong></p>
<p>Our teams and third-party specialists continue investigating, remediating, and validating services for safe restoration. Published findings and partner guidance remain current.</p>
<p>Containment remains in place, with no successful threat activity observed in monitored environments since mitigations initiated October 17, 05:00 UTC. We are monitoring our entire environment, with no indication of impact beyond Cloud Backup and the precautionary suspensions of SaaS Security and Cloud Management. All three services remain suspended.</p>
<p>We recognize the disruption to your business and customers. We will share restoration timing and reconnection instructions as soon as confirmed.</p>
<p id="video"><strong>Actions for partners</strong></p>
<p>Follow the <a aria-label="Link technical investigation and remediation guide" id="menur55uc" href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf">technical investigation and remediation guide</a> for your Microsoft 365 tenant and each managed customer tenant. Keep affected applications disabled pending restoration instructions.</p>
<p><strong>For a step-by-step walkthrough of the technical investigation and remediation guide, watch the video.<br /><br /></strong></p>
<p><strong>Important Security Guidance</strong></p>
<p>This video illustrates selected steps from ConnectWise's Cloud Backup Technical Investigation and Remediation Guide and is intended for authorized IT administrators and security professionals.</p>
<p>Before making changes, preserve relevant evidence, validate findings, and assess potential operational impacts. Completing these steps does not guarantee that a tenant is unaffected or that all unauthorized access has been eliminated. <strong>Do not reconnect affected applications until ConnectWise provides formal restoration instructions.</strong> Please continue to refer to the ConnectWise Trust Center for the latest guidance.&nbsp;It is intended for administrators and security teams reviewing their own and customer Microsoft 365 tenants and should be used alongside the written guide.</p>
