<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-19-1345-utc"><em><br /><br /></em><span style="color: #24326a;"><strong>Update: Monday, October 19, 2026 at 13:45 UTC</strong></span><em><br /></em><span style="color: #24326a;"><strong></strong></span></p>
<p><span><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update</strong></span></p>
<p><span>The findings and partner guidance shared previously remain current as of this update.</span></p>
<p><span>Our incident response, engineering, and operations teams continue advancing the investigation and remediation with third-party specialists. This work includes validating findings, verifying containment measures, and completing the security checks needed to restore services safely. We are responsible for this work and for keeping you informed.</span></p>
<p><span>Containment measures remain in place. Since implementing mitigations, we have not observed successful threat activity in the environments we monitor since October 17, 05:00 UTC.</span></p>
<p><span>Cloud Backup, SaaS Security, and Cloud Management remain suspended. Scheduled backups, archive access, and restores remain unavailable, along with SaaS Security monitoring and alerting and Cloud Management user and license management.</span></p>
<p><span>We recognize the continued disruption to your operations and your customers. Our teams remain focused on restoring service safely. We do not yet have a confirmed restoration time and will share a timeline and any required reconnection instructions as soon as they are confirmed.</span></p>
<p><span><strong>Actions for partners</strong></span></p>
<p><span>Please continue following the </span><a aria-label="Link Cloud Backup technical investigation and remediation guide" id="menur3iol" href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf"><span>Cloud Backup technical investigation and remediation guide</span></a><span>. Review your own Microsoft 365 tenant and each customer tenant you manage, and keep affected applications disabled pending formal restoration instructions.</span></p>
<p><span>If you provide services through a reseller, distributor, or marketplace, ensure the administrator responsible for each customer tenant receives and acts on this guidance.</span></p>
