<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-18-1845-utc"><span style="color: #24326a;"><strong>Update: Sunday, October 18, 2026 at 18:45 UTC<br /></strong></span></p>
<h6><span><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update</strong></span></h6>
<p><span>We are continuing our investigation and remediation following unauthorized access to application identities associated with ConnectWise Cloud Backup, formerly known as SkyKick.</span></p>
<p><span>Our investigation and remediation remain ongoing, and our incident response, engineering, and operations teams continue working around the clock with third-party specialists to restore service safely and as quickly as possible.</span></p>
<p><span>For partners using the former SkyKick services, <strong>Cloud Backup</strong> is currently suspended in response to observed indicators of unauthorized activity. Because <strong>SaaS Security and Cloud Management</strong> are integrated with Cloud Backup, we also suspended those services out of an abundance of caution while our investigation and remediation continue</span></p>
<p><span>We recognize the continued disruption to your business and your customers, particularly while backup and restoration services remain unavailable.</span></p>
<h6><span><strong>Additional IP Indicators</strong></span></h6>
<p><span>The following IP addresses were shared with us through downstream security monitoring of partner and customer environments. Partners should include these addresses when reviewing available Microsoft 365 authentication and audit logs.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span>144.172.64[.]99 <strong>NEW</strong></span></li>
<li><span>144.172.64[.]60 <strong>NEW</strong></span></li>
<li><span>144.172.64[.]128 <strong>PREVIOUSLY LISTED</strong></span></li>
</ul>
<h6><span><strong><br />Detailed guidance for partners and customer administrators</strong></span></h6>
<p><span>Our previously published guidance remains in effect. The </span><a href="/contentassets/10777cd3364d440c86ed5270a94a5f24/connectwise-cloud-backup-technical-investigation-and-remediation-guide-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span><strong>Cloud Backup technical investigation and remediation guide</strong></span></a><span>&nbsp;provides detailed instructions for reviewing your MSP&rsquo;s Microsoft 365 environment and each customer environment you manage. It covers affected application identities, sign-in and audit records, credentials, permissions, role assignments, and potential persistence through other identities or mailbox changes.</span></p>
<p><span><strong>If you provide these services through a reseller, distributor, or marketplace arrangement, ensure this guidance reaches the administrator responsible for each customer tenant.</strong> If you do not administer those environments directly, coordinate with the customer&rsquo;s IT administrator or security provider to confirm that the guidance has been received and the review is being addressed.</span></p>
<p><span>We will continue publishing updates, including when there is no material change. <strong>Our next update will be posted by 1:00 UTC on October 19, 2026.</strong></span></p>
<p><span>Please use the </span><a aria-label="Link ConnectWise Trust Center" id="menur2v78" href="/company/trust/advisories" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories"><span>ConnectWise Trust Center</span></a><span> for current status and guidance. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to </span><a aria-label="Link SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" id="menur2v7b" href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="mailto:securitypartnersupport@connectwise.com"><span><strong>SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</strong></span></a><span>.</span></p>
<p><br /><br /></p>
<p id="cloud-backup-update-2026-10-18-1600-utc"><span style="color: #24326a;"><strong><br /><br />Update: Sunday, October 18, 2026 at 16:00 UTC</strong></span></p>
<h6><span><strong>Cloud Backup service interruption update</strong></span></h6>
<p><span>We are continuing our investigation and remediation following unauthorized access to application identities associated with ConnectWise Cloud Backup, formerly known as SkyKick.</span></p>
<p>At this time, we have no new confirmed findings to report. Our previously published guidance remains unchanged and is available <a href="#october-18-update">here</a>.&nbsp;We are contacting our entire partner base to ensure all partners are aware of the incident, the protective actions we have taken, and where to find current guidance.</p>
<p><span>For partners using the former SkyKick services, we suspended <strong>Cloud Backup</strong> in response to observed indicators of unauthorized activity. Because <strong>SaaS Security and Cloud Management</strong> are integrated with Cloud Backup, we also suspended those services out of an abundance of caution while our investigation and remediation continue. Cloud Backup jobs, archive access, and restores remain unavailable, as do SaaS Security monitoring and alerting and Cloud Management user and license management.</span></p>
<p><span>We have implemented containment measures and engaged third-party incident response specialists. Our teams continue monitoring the affected environments, conducting forensic analysis and threat hunting, and carrying out remediation. We are validating the effectiveness of these measures to support a controlled restoration of service.</span></p>
<p><span><strong>Existing backup archives remain encrypted and isolated, and we have no indication that those archives have been compromised.</strong> These findings concern stored backup archives and do not establish whether individual live Microsoft 365 environments were affected. Partners should continue following the published guidance at </span><a aria-label="Link ConnectWise Trust Center" id="menur2l1o" href="/company/trust/advisories" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="https://www.connectwise.com/company/trust/advisories"><span>ConnectWise Trust Center</span></a><span> with their security teams or managed security providers.</span></p>
<p><span>Our incident response, engineering, and operations teams are working around the clock to restore service. We recognize the disruption this continues to cause our partners and their customers. Restoring service safely remains our top priority.</span></p>
<p><span>We will continue publishing updates, including when there is no material change. <strong>Our next update will be posted by 19:00 UTC on October 18, 2026.</strong></span></p>
<p><span>Please use the Trust Center for current status and guidance. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to </span><a aria-label="Link SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" id="menur2l1r" href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" class="fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn" title="mailto:securitypartnersupport@connectwise.com"><span><strong>SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</strong></span></a><span>.</span></p>
<p id="october-18-update"><em><br /><br /></em><span style="color: #24326a;"><strong>Update: Sunday, October 18, 2026 at 01:00 UTC</strong></span><em><br /></em></p>
<h6><strong>Cloud Backup investigation and service update</strong></h6>
<p>We are continuing our investigation and remediation following unauthorized access to application identities associated with ConnectWise Cloud Backup, formerly known as SkyKick. This update provides more detail on the actions we have taken, the services currently unavailable, and the suggested system checks partners should complete in their Microsoft 365 environments.</p>
<h6><strong>Actions taken by ConnectWise</strong></h6>
<p>At 07:00 UTC on October 17, 2026, we disabled the seven ConnectWise application identities listed in the technical guidance below. Disabling the affected connections prevents new authentication through those connections; it does not reverse changes previously made inside a tenant.</p>
<p>We also suspended Cloud Backup service by revoking certificates used for affected application connections. The affected shared Cloud Backup credentials are no longer valid. Previously issued access tokens may remain usable until they expire or are otherwise invalidated. Any unauthorized credentials, permissions, or other access established through separate identities require additional review and remediation.</p>
<p>In addition to mobilizing our internal security teams and Security Operations Center, we engaged a reputable third-party forensics firm. Together, these teams continue monitoring our backup infrastructure and broader environment. We are also reviewing other potentially affected partner facing services. Since implementing our mitigations, we have not observed successful threat activity in the environments we monitor. Investigation and validation remain ongoing.</p>
<p>We are still in the investigation stage of our incident response process, validating critical findings and mitigation paths. We do not have a restoration time to share yet. We will advise partners when we exit this phase and provide reconnection or reauthorization instructions as soon as they are confirmed.</p>
<h6><strong>Service availability and backup data</strong></h6>
<p>Cloud Backup remains suspended. Scheduled backups are not running, and access to affected backup archives and restoration capabilities remains unavailable. Existing archives remain encrypted, isolated, and preserved. We have no evidence that these archives have been accessed.</p>
<p>As an additional precaution, we have temporarily taken <strong>SaaS Security and Cloud Management</strong> offline while we complete our review. During this pause, SaaS Security monitoring and alerting and Cloud Management user and license management are unavailable. Please contact Partner Care for assistance with changes you would normally make through these services.</p>
<p>These service interruptions are proactive, protective actions. They do not, by themselves, establish that a partner or customer environment was compromised. We will communicate service-specific restoration status as our review progresses.</p>
<h6><strong>Actions partners should take</strong></h6>
<p>Partners should review both <strong>their own Microsoft 365 tenant and each managed customer tenant</strong>, including environments with dormant SkyKick connections. Work with your security team or managed security provider to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Verify the status of the listed application connections and keep affected applications disabled until ConnectWise provides restoration instructions.</li>
<li>Preserve available sign-in and audit records promptly, while taking any urgent containment action.</li>
<li>Review application and user authentication, application credentials and federation trusts, directory roles, owners, consent grants, and recent policy changes.</li>
<li>Check for unauthorized mailbox forwarding, inbox or transport rules, and delegated mailbox access.</li>
<li>Investigate any other identities changed or used during suspicious activity; disabling the original applications does not remove those separate access paths.</li>
</ul>
<p>The detailed workflow below explains where to look, what findings need investigation, and how to coordinate remediation. A successful sign-in alone does not establish that data was copied. Equally, a clean search cannot rule out activity that was not captured in the available logs.</p>
<p>Our findings about stored archives are separate from potential activity in live Microsoft 365 environments. Cloud Backup does not provide the downstream security visibility needed for us to determine independently whether a particular partner or customer tenant experienced unauthorized activity. The tenant review is therefore an important part of the response.</p>
<h6><strong>Communications and next update</strong></h6>
<p>We have published incident updates and guidance through the Trust Center and contacted partners through email and direct calls. We have also posted updates on LinkedIn and Reddit. We will continue using these channels to share material findings, service status, and required partner actions.</p>
<p>We appreciate the cybersecurity community&rsquo;s support and contributions to the investigation. We recognize the urgency of restoring protection for our partners and their customers and are working urgently toward that goal.</p>
<p>We will continue to publish updates to the Trust Center, including if there is no material change. Please use the Trust Center for current status and guidance. Contact Partner Care for service assistance and report suspicious activity to <a href="mailto:SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com">SecurityPartnerSupport@ConnectWise.com</a>.</p>
<h6><strong>Technical workflow for MSPs and customer administrators</strong></h6>
<p>We recommend that partners complete the following actions, working with their security team and following relevant Microsoft guidance.</p>
<p>Complete this review in your MSP tenant and each customer tenant you manage. Use an authorized account and involve your security team or incident response provider. Log access, application administration, directory-role changes, policy management, and Exchange investigation require different permissions; Global Administrator or Privileged Role Administrator is not a blanket prerequisite for every check.</p>
<h6><strong>Application identities disabled on October 17</strong></h6>
<p>ConnectWise disabled the following seven application identities at 07:00 UTC. Partners should still verify each local enterprise-application setting. A vendor action and a customer-tenant setting are different controls; this table does not document a separate local change in every customer tenant.<br /><br /></p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-spacing: 0px; background-color: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #000000;" border="1">
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col" style="border-color: #000000; border-width: 1px; padding: 12px;"><strong>Application</strong></th>
